# Frontend-only artifacts. Companion to backend/.gitignore: the root file keeps
# only what is shared across the repo, and each subtree's .gitignore owns what
# is uniquely its own. The root entries this file replaces were anchored
# ("/.svelte-kit"), so they never matched anything in frontend/ -- the rule
# that actually worked was a "/frontend/.svelte-kit" line appended at the
# bottom of the root file. These are the same patterns, unanchored, so they
# resolve relative to frontend/.
#
# Env-file rules (.env, .env.*, !.env.example) deliberately stay in the root
# .gitignore. They are shared with backend/, and the deeper file takes
# precedence over the root rather than merging with it: duplicating them here
# would mean two files that must stay byte-identical, and any drift would
# re-ignore a tracked .env.example with no error.

# deps
node_modules/

# svelte-kit
.svelte-kit/
build/
.output/
.vercel/
.netlify/
.wrangler/

# vite
vite.config.js.timestamp-*
vite.config.ts.timestamp-*

# test coverage
coverage/